# This repo was split out of a larger one whose .gitignore lived at its
# root and did not travel with it. Without this file, `git add -A` commits
# the Terraform provider cache (a ~600MB binary) and terraform.tfstate.

# Terraform: the provider cache is re-downloadable, and state is both
# environment-specific and a place secrets end up.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
# Lambda zips, and the directory deploy.sh assembles the queue runner in:
# a copy of src/ppe_pipeline_api plus PyYAML, rebuilt on every deploy.
# Committing it would put a second, silently diverging copy of the
# application source in the repo.
terraform/*/.build/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node / frontend build output -- the image builds its own.
node_modules/
web/dist/

# Local environment and editor noise
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
*.log
